User sent in a report regarding their second monitor not turning on and giving a "No Signal" message when they turn on their devices.
It was working the day before. Power goes to the monitor, it just won't show any visuals nor gets detected.

The user has done some troubleshooting on their own and given the following report:
- Checked all the cables are plugged in
- Swapped in a different cable and tried the other video port on my PC - still "No Signal"
- Restarted the computer
- Borrowed a coworker's laptop to test the monitor - works on theirs

This means that we need to remote Desktop into their device and continue the investigation.

When on their desktop, I can see artifacts on graphical glitches happening.
I right click on the desktop and I find the Display adapter showing an error/warning:

Basic Display Adapter.
This adapter may not support multiple displays.

We will head into the System Update app next and check for updates.

We see there's different drivers that needs an update, so we go through the list.
Some of them needing a restart after update, but this solved the problem and the user can see their monitor working again
and proceed their tasks.

Ticket solved.
